  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Designing locally led humanitarian response in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This work will build on and add to existing work, funded by philanthropy, that the Share Trust is doing to unpack examples of good locally led action by a range of intermediary actors in Sudan, understand the incentives/structures donors set that help enable (or detract from) intermediaries&apos; efforts to advance locally led action, and explore the comparative advantages of the range of different intermediaries in fulfilling different functions (e.g., devolving funding and power to local levels, managing compliance, yielding cost efficiencies, implementing programmatic approaches, achieving results).</narrative>
  </description>
